lines=['# R01 Task 6 Fix1 — known-function metadata rejection','',f'Fix execution parent `{base}`. Source-only I1/I2 fix; controller same-reviewer acceptance and exact-head CI are pending. No PR publication, production apply/deploy/enable, Task1 SQL or Task7 work.', '',f'Final SQL `{sql}`: {len(current):,} bytes; SHA256 `{proof["sqlSHA256"]}`. Final runner SHA256 `{host["testedExecutableBlobs"]["supabase/rls-tests/helpers/runR01CrmForward.ts"]["sha256"]}`. Candidate tree and packaging meaning are in `task-6-fix-1-source-binding.json`; packaging HEAD is the commit containing this report/binding, distinct from the execution parent.','', '## Implementation and self-review','', 'I1 binds postgres ownership and the complete effective ACL (including grantor, recipient, EXECUTE, and no grant option) of both existing version helpers. The ordinary helper stays postgres-only; the role helper keeps its historical PUBLIC/postgres effective ACL. Existing hosted/modern exact definition hashes remain. I2 requires pronargdefaults=0 and proargdefaults IS NULL for all five existing command/bridge profiles. Unknown metadata fails55000 before definitions. The authoritative generator and manifest are synchronized. No historical SQL/shared helper/Auth/table grant/default normalization or runtime HTTP change.', '', 'The full SQL definition/grant tail after the preflight marker is byte-identical to 7f. Public/private bodies, signatures, owner, ACL, and actor/version/consent/audit behavior remain unchanged. DB test/HTTP source/tests and productionSchemaClone remain unchanged. The new runner has seven helper owner/recipient/grant-option/PUBLIC fixtures and five otherwise-identical default fixtures. Default fixtures compare the full pg_proc metadata excluding the two changed default fields; helper fixtures retain exact definition hashes. Existing roles only, transaction-local changes and forced rollback; owner transfer uses the already-authorized clone session owner. No cluster roles/memberships.', '', '## Actual failure-first reproduction and retained failed attempts','', '`$env:R01_CRM_ALLOW_LOCAL_FIXTURES="1"; bun run docs/evidence/audit-remediation-20260927/r01-forward/task-6-fix-1-red.ts red` exit1. `red.json` UTC '+red['startedAt']+' to '+red['completedAt']+'. Accepted positive baseline plus forced rollback passed before negatives. Exact archived original7f SQL wrongly accepted all12 actual owner/ACL/default fixtures; each setupComplete and full-preservation check passed. Actual owner ACL grant-option transition false→true is recorded; helper definition hashes and default-body hashes remain. This actual RED follows the earlier static review finding; it is not a claim that review executed a DB test. Fresh synthetic clone normal DROP; template/modern/frozen true.', '', '- Initial pool-max1 fixture starvation: the fixture queried a global client while holding its transaction connection. No migration verdict/domain RED. Exact initial runner/log/process/diagnostic receipts retained. Only verified owned Bun36988/parent35968 was stopped; command exit−1. `bun run docs/evidence/audit-remediation-20260927/r01-forward/task-6-fix-1-cleanup.ts` exit0 verified complete catalog/rows/Auth-table+column ACL/all defaults/native dependencies/ledger/source/template/modern hashes equal before/after connection-close rollback and used normal owned DROP, no FORCE or PG backend termination. Corrected only fixture to the held transaction client after cleanup.', '- Source edit-script marker assertion is qualified in edit-script-attempt-qualification.json; not DB/domain evidence.', '- First GREEN setup attempt exit1: valid baseline/rollback and original49 refusals, then owner transfer under SET ROLE postgres failed42501 before migration. Exact first-green-owner-fixture runner/log/JSON retained; template/modern/frozen true and normal DROP. Changed only the fixture to use the legal existing session owner before migration switches postgres.', '- Preformat both DB runs exited0 (61 refusals/25pass205assert each), but their composition is superseded. First four gates: typecheck0/39.14s; tests0/85.32s (3235pass292skip0fail10499assert); lint1/40.24s, solely29 Prettier errors in the new runner block plus52 baseline warnings; build0/59.48s; wrapper exit1/frozen true. All preformat logs/source/receipts/DB maps retained separately. No input edited until build closed. `bun node_modules/prettier/bin/prettier.cjs --write supabase/rls-tests/helpers/runR01CrmForward.ts` exit0/428ms; focused `bun node_modules/eslint/bin/eslint.js supabase/rls-tests/helpers/runR01CrmForward.ts` exit0. Both profiles and four gates were required and rerun after the runner bytes changed; no exemption used.', '', '## Final frozen database validation','', '`$env:R01_CRM_ALLOW_LOCAL_FIXTURES="1"; bun run supabase/rls-tests/helpers/runR01CrmForward.ts green` exit0; corresponding `green-modern` command exit0. Child exact `bun test src/lib/crm/atomicForward.database.test.ts --timeout 30000` exit0 in each owned clone. Final hosted UTC '+host['startedAt']+' to '+host['completedAt']+'; modern UTC '+modern['startedAt']+' to '+modern['completedAt']+'. Both use identical24 actual observed inputs and current HTTP bytes. Each: accepted baseline/rollback, all61 preserved55000 (49original+12Fix1; new fixtures setupComplete with exact helper/function-contract errors), two applies,25pass205assert0fail, temp shadows and all existing concurrency/role drift/audit rollback/retry tests. Hosted25→22 after accepted Tasks2–5; modern1→1. Fresh zero-data application tables158/162; all catalog/related-unrelated rows/fullAuth ACLs/defaults/native16+dependencies/ledger/source preserved and normal DROP. Task1 excluded. No production actor/data/DDL; capture uses schema/catalog read-only.', '', '## Final four local gates','', '`C:/Python314/python.exe docs/evidence/audit-remediation-20260927/r01-forward/task-6-fix-1-gates.py final` exit0. It removes inherited *TEST_DATABASE_URL/*ALLOW_LOCAL_FIXTURES, uses loopback DB57322/Auth52321 and only build54329/ci-placeholder keys. All30 final gate input hashes remain equal. Raw receipt `task-6-fix-1-receipts/task-6-final-gates.json`; UTC '+g['startedAt']+' to '+g['completedAt']+'.','']
for x in g['gates']:lines.append(f'- `{x["command"]}`: exit{x["exit"]}, {x["elapsedSeconds"]}s.'+(' 3235pass/292skip/0fail/10499assertions.' if x['gate']=='tests' else ' Existing52 baseline warnings/M1 deferred.' if x['gate']=='lint' else ''))
